      "side": 1,
      "message": "`jgit` is handled differently because it is an actual Bazel module: it has module metadata and contributes to bzlmod resolution, including the shared Maven graph.\n\nSo the correct pattern is `bazel_dep(name \u003d \"jgit\")` plus `local_path_override(...)` to point that module at our in-tree checkout.\n\n`java-prettify` is not a bzlmod module. It does not participate in module resolution and does not contribute module metadata; it is just a local source repository with `BUILD` files. For that case, `local_repository(...)` is the appropriate mechanism.\n\nSo the distinction is not really “has external deps vs not”, but “is a real Bazel module vs just a repository”. If `java-prettify` is ever converted into a proper Bazel module, we could treat it the same way as `jgit`.",
